@*
    OdsLocationSelect — THE place picker (Odyssey Design System · components/LocationSelect, issue #383 §4).

    Wherever a record links a household Location — the Place of a calendar event, a recurring series or
    a journal entry, and the place behind a contact or property address. It is the place counterpart of
    OdsContactSelect: OdsCombobox in its ASYNC mode inside the standard field chrome.

    Search runs server-side (GET /api/locations?search=, 20 per request) after 2 characters and a
    250 ms pause; never the unpaged list. Active places only — archived and merged-away places are never
    offered for a new link — while a stored value outside the loaded rows, archived ones included,
    still renders through ResolveAsync and reads "‹name› (archived)".

    Value is a LocationPick: an existing place by id, or a STAGED new one. With AllowCreate (the caller
    gates it on locations.create) the list ends with Create place "‹text›", whose second line discloses
    who will see the place. Picking it calls no API: the trigger reads "‹name› (new)" and the PARENT
    creates the place when its own dialog saves (PlaceDraft.EnsureCreatedAsync).

    With AllowCreate the place picker also searches Kartverket (issue #383 v6 §3.2a): the rows are grouped "Saved
    places" (every active place) and "Addresses from Kartverket", under the same search, debounce, failure note,
    dedupe and disclosure as address mode below — one implementation, not a copy — and the create row still ends
    the list. Only the failure note differs, since there is no hand-entry row: "Address search is unavailable —
    pick a saved place or create one". A Kartverket pick is LocationPick.Address(candidate), staged as "‹address› (new)"; the parent creates
    it as a geocoded place when its dialog saves (PlaceDraft.EnsureCreatedAsync).

    ADDRESS MODE (Mode=Address, issue #383 v5 §3.3a) is the one Address field of a contact or property: label
    "Address", address-complete places only, no create row, and the rows in two labelled groups — "Saved places"
    (each "used by N") and, with AllowCreate (locations.create), "Addresses from Kartverket": from 3 characters
    and a 400 ms pause the query also goes to POST /api/locations/search, region Norway, and only address results
    are listed, less any whose address equals a listed saved place. Picking one STAGES it ("‹address› (new)"):
    the value is LocationPick.Address(candidate) and nothing is created until the record saves. A failed address
    search says "Address search is unavailable — enter the address by hand" in its group; a cancelled one is
    silent. The final row, "Enter an address by hand…", calls OnEnterByHand with the typed text. Under the field,
    always visible while the address search is on and part of the input's description: "Address search sends
    what you type to Kartverket."

    A caller without locations.read does not render this component at all (no placeholder, no disabled
    control) — that is the caller's rule, not this component's.
*@

@if (Bare)
{
    @Control
    @Disclosure
}
else
{
    <OdsFieldShell Label="@EffectiveLabel" HtmlFor="@_inputId" Required="@Required" Help="@Help" Error="@Error" Class="odc-locsel">
        @Control
    </OdsFieldShell>
    @Disclosure
}

@code {
    private RenderFragment Control =>
        @<OdsCombobox Value="@ComboValue"
                      ValueChanged="OnValueChanged"
                      Options="CurrentOptions"
                      Placeholder="@EffectivePlaceholder"
                      Disabled="@Disabled"
                      Clearable="true"
                      ClearLabel="@(IsAddressMode ? "Clear address" : "Clear place")"
                      InputId="@_inputId"
                      AriaLabel="@(Bare ? AriaLabel ?? EffectiveLabel : null)"
                      AriaDescribedBy="@DescribedBy"
                      Required="@Required"
                      Error="@(!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Error))"
                      EmptyText="@EffectiveEmptyText"
                      SearchAsync="SearchAsync"
                      ResolveAsync="ResolveAsync"
                      DebounceMs="@DebounceMs"
                      MinChars="2"
                      MinCharsText="Type at least 2 characters"
                      SearchingText="Searching…"
                      ResultsText="@(IsAddressMode ? n => $"{n} {(n == 1 ? "address" : "addresses")} found" : n => $"{n} {(n == 1 ? "place" : "places")} found")"
                      ErrorText="Couldn’t load places"
                      OnCreate="@(AllowCreate && !IsAddressMode ? Stage : null)"
                      CreateLabel="Create place"
                      CreateDescription="@(AllowCreate && !IsAddressMode ? CreateDisclosure : null)"
                      Groups="@(Grouped ? AddressGroups : null)"
                      FooterOption="@Footer" />;

    private RenderFragment? Disclosure => !AddressSearchOn ? null :
        @<div class="odc-locsel-disclose" id="@DisclosureId">
            <span class="material-icons" aria-hidden="true">info</span>
            <span>@AddressSearchDisclosure</span>
        </div>;
}
